diff --git a/docs/auto-root-apps-20261031/README.md b/docs/auto-root-apps-20261031/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..37254a90ed79a44032431836c390be211008f100
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/auto-root-apps-20261031/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,92 @@
+# Automatic protection of root-related apps
+
+Extends the reviewed PR #158 priority filter (Samsung parent `fc114e5`) with the
+scope requested by the maintainer: RMGU, installed root managers, and apps granted
+root. The existing four native/compat operations and caller exclusions remain.
+
+## Live kernel policy
+
+A single immutable RCU rules object holds the explicit manager bitmap, automatic
+mode and RMGU app ID. Readers first check the bitmap, then RMGU's app ID or the
+backend's live `ksu_is_uid_granted_root(target_uid)` predicate. The latter includes
+the registered manager. Grants, revocations and manager registration changes take
+effect without polling, package lookup, allocation or credential changes. It uses
+the exact target UID for per-user root grants; own/explicit app IDs apply across
+Android users, as in the earlier filter. Sharing an app ID cannot be separated.
+Trusted KernelSU profiles, root/system and self queries keep their normal behavior.
+
+All four exact bundled backend pins expose the same `bool(uid_t)` root predicate
+and behavior (recorded in `records/backend-policy.json`). Targets are app IDs
+10000..19999, so the predicate's context-sensitive UID-zero special case is never
+reached. SusFS accesses no private allowlist structures. The existing allowlist's
+non-sleeping read path supplies grant decisions inside the RCU read section.
+
+Both KSU policy pointers are resolved while preemption is disabled, with the
+owning module retained before either is published. The root pointer must belong
+to the same owner as the umount predicate. An ownerless pointer requires an exact
+vmlinux symbol match. Unknown ownership, a going module or missing root predicate
+leaves automatic selection unavailable. The reference is released only after all
+SusFS feature exits, hook drains and a final Tasks-RCU grace period. This also
+repairs the old umount pointer lifetime. While SusFS is active, its backend must
+remain loaded. A full reboot is the supported way to switch these modules.
+
+## Configuration and Android integration
+
+The existing standard `0x60030` ABI is unchanged: a transactional package-list
+replacement. It now replaces only explicit extras, preserving automatic mode.
+`clear` clears those extras; it does not turn automatic mode off.
+
+The root-only private command `0x6f001` accepts `{ unsigned int enabled;
+unsigned int own_appid; int err; }` (12 bytes, error offset 8). Enable requires
+1 and an app ID in 10000..19999; disable requires both fields zero. It preserves
+the explicit bitmap and refuses configuration if the optional hook layer failed.
+The freestanding client exposes `auto <app_id>` and `auto-off`. Existing manual
+usage still works with automatic mode off. No upstream feature bit was invented.
+
+RMGU passes read-only (0400) `priority_auto_root=1 priority_appid=<own app ID>`
+parameters at load, enabling the live policy before successful activation. Missing
+policy support disables only this optional automatic feature. A read-only status
+reports ready, configured, generation, automatic, own_appid and root_lookup. The
+app verifies mode/ownership and can enable it on an already loaded new module.
+An older live module needs a full reboot after the APK update.
+
+Only after unlock, a coalesced Android JobService inventories installed known or
+structurally recognized managers, including renamed managers found by the existing
+APK/daemon scanner and the user's manager choice. It resolves fresh names each
+time; no numeric UID list is persisted. Boot/unlock, app resume, supported removal
+broadcasts and dynamic package-change receivers request a refresh. Android does
+not deliver every install broadcast to a stopped background process: a newly
+installed inactive manager can wait until the next app open/activation/unlock.
+The active registered manager and granted-root apps are protected immediately by
+the kernel regardless of whether RMGU's process is running. There is no timer or
+recurring grant scan, and package inventory does not delay early root.
+
+The background worker uses bounded direct `su`, a cross-process configuration
+lock and a current-boot device-protected JSON record. It publishes a whole fresh
+manager list. A confirmed native failure can clear stale extras and retry once;
+a timeout is indeterminate and triggers no competing fallback command. Status
+shows automatic protection or an update/full-reboot hint, without a confirmation
+screen. Core SusFS status is independent of this optional feature.
+
+## Validation
+
+29 host suites / 56 normal and sanitizer configurations pass. Production-C tests
+cover live grants/revocations, per-user decisions, own ID, manual coexistence,
+invalid/unsupported commands, read-only boot parameters, initialization failure,
+concurrent bitmap/automatic writers/readers and RCU retirement. Dependency tests
+cover built-in/module ownership, missing/foreign/going providers and grace/ref
+lifetime; five deliberately unsafe mutants must fail. Lifecycle tests cover root
+admission and refusal of both priority commands when the optional layer fails.
+
+The Android16/6.12 ARM64 DDK module and freestanding client build successfully.
+All 22 syscall wrappers match real-header CFI types and valid landing instructions;
+baseline imports, callback types and version table shape remain intact. Only
+`_ctype`, `strim`, `strsep` and `preempt_schedule` are added to the stable module's
+imports. All 140 imported names and the dynamically resolved module-owner helper
+exist in the recovered BZJA kernel. Its actual I/O-priority validation still
+matches the callable helper. Metadata changes only by the two parameter types.
+Records pin the exact source hashes and distributed bytes. These are static/host
+checks, not complete ABI proof or phone validation. Hardware validation is pending.
+
+See the app repository's `docs/susfs-priority-filter-20261030.md` for test APK and
+rollback instructions. Full source, tests and previous evidence are retained.
