new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..a7724991771d97b790f388c5e765d2e591e56bad
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/priority_filter/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+# Priority filter host checks
+
+The runner compiles the entire production priority layer with modeled allocation,
+VFS ownership, credentials, native/compat original handlers, callback counts and
+RCU reader grace periods. Both compat-enabled and native-only configurations run.
+Cases cover transactional replacement/clear, shared UID deduplication, invalid
+names and owners, lookup/allocator/copy faults, unterminated payloads, exact UID
+and namespace gates, preserved arguments and return values, I/O validation error
+ordering, partial installation rollback, sleeping teardown and concurrent writers.
+Caller cases also cover SDK sandbox and app-zygote UID boundaries in multiple
+Android users, across all eight syscall entries, with trusted-profile passthrough.
+
+Negative controls remove compat separation, validation, path checks, callback
+admission, complete compat coverage, or SDK/app-zygote caller coverage. The
+sanitizer run also reintroduces a publication-lifetime bug. Each control must be detected. These models do not
+establish live kernel behavior or Samsung protected-memory compatibility.
